WEBVTT

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:04.930
Hold it!

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.560
Are you sure you shouldn't call Misuzu 
and the others for backup, Chuta?

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.410
I can handle an incident 
like this on my own.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.980
And I'm not in 
Investigations Division 2 right now.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.820
I'm going to Investigations Division 4?

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.010
Division 4's had some 
openings for a while now.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:23.950
It's just a temporary assignment.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.430
Who's in Division 4?

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.370
Come to think of it, I don't know of anyone.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.640
Inspector Vega from Division 4 is 
hurrying to the scene of the crime right now.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.550
Please hurry and head over there, too.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.060
Yoyosa!

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:39.670
Chuta!

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.490
Yeah!

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.770
This is ēlDLIVE! You have the right to...

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.850
I forgot my badge!

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.810
Chuta!

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:53.680
Hold it!

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.940
SPH...

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:00.910
He's a fast one...

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.160
Then we should use that.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:02.700
Yeah.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:04.420
Sympathy!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.200
Freezing gum off!

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:08.950
Tch!

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.410
You can't escape!

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.040
Huh?!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.250
That's a body substitution technique.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.880
You're finished, ēlDLIVE.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.420
Thank goodness I made it in time.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:37.600
Reinforcements?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.440
Are you hurt, Officer Kokonose?

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:47.370
I'm Inspector Vega Victor from the ēlDLIVE 
Solar System Bureau Investigations Division 4.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.180
<b>Your Voice...</b>

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.970
Inspector Vega Victor?

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.370
So he's the head of Division 4?

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.100
SPH... Luce Bomber!

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:36.300
SPH Rosso Assalto.

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:42.110
You should give up.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.850
You're just going to add to your crimes.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.420
I messed up...

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.050
I guess this is the end for me.

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.630
Chuta, it's that mark.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.000
DeMille...

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.660
Come on, kill me!

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:07.750
I'm just going to be eliminated anyway!

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:12.190
Knowing everything you've done,
 I would love to simply kill you.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:15.410
I even have that authority.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:17.600
But...

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.480
He's going to explode, Chuta!

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.190
Look out!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.360
...I won't allow you to die.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.210
You're going to live 
and atone for your crimes.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.640
Wow...

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.170
We don't have enough personnel 
in our division right now.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:49.390
I know it's only temporary, but it's a 
great help that you've come to Division 4.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:54.140
Um... Section Chief Vega... 
I'd also like to thank you for today.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.470
Huh? For what?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.220
You saved me from a tight spot...

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.140
Oh, that. Don't worry about it.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.230
But if you hadn't arrived back then, I...

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.790
It's only natural for a senior agent 
to help out a junior agent, right?

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.740
We're part of the 
Investigations Division 4 team.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.280
Chuta!

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:15.870
Yes!

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.910
We're also close in age, so I'm going 
to call you Chuta from now on.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.260
So you can just call me Vega, too.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.410
No need to be so formal.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:25.500
Yes...

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.370
You're so stiff. You can just say "yeah."

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:29.420
Okay.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:30.500
Good!

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:35.060
There's a warm feeling 
welling up inside you, Chuta.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:38.900
It's like the feeling you have for Mimi, 
but slightly different.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:44.000
I wonder if this is what it feels like 
to have a brother.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:48.660
<b>Shirobori Middle School</b>

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.950
Chuta!

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.530
Want to go to the art museum this weekend?

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.580
The art museum?

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.350
I glanced at the poster for the exhibit 
they're doing right now, and it's awesome!

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.850
Takkun said he'd go, too.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.840
Yeah, sure. That's fine...

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.190
Tateyan wants to go to the art museum?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.680
That's rather surprising.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.640
Misuzu, you've been sneaking after Chuta lately.
What are you up to?

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.320
I'm not being sneaky.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.770
Oh, my. Who's that?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.990
That hot guy!

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:26.270
Toku-chan, calm down.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:31.490
Vega.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.460
Hey, Chuta.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.820
You know him, Chuta?

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.470
Y-Yeah... U-Um...

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.290
I'm Chuta's cousin, Vega.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:41.460
Nice to meet you.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.820
Vega?

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.330
That's a cool name!

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.120
I wonder if he's a high school student.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:47.790
We got a hottie in glasses here!

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.620
It seems that Chuta-san and Vega-san 
are getting along very well.

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.790
Misuzu, aren't you lonely 
without Chuta around?

00:06:55.670 --> 00:06:57.930
It's time to go to work, 
so please excuse me.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:09.200
Which means... the reason for 
the smell was because of me...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.150
What's at the foundation of this is a 
sense of annoyance towards yourself.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:18.010
When you saw Chuta maturing next to you, 
your urge to mature yourself also intensified.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.170
That's a very natural thing.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:23.830
Misuzu!

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.390
Have you seen Chuta?

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.280
No...

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:31.080
Well, when you do see him, 
could you give him this?

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.050
I wanted to give him this earlier,

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.760
but it took a while to get 
clearance from the higher-ups.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.580
I'm sorry for all of the trouble 
I caused about the smell.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:47.420
I'm sorry for all of the trouble 
I caused about the smell.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.230
Okay.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.900
Officer Kokonose.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.780
Hello, Officer Sonokata. 
Did you need something from Chuta?

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.370
No. It's nothing important.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.220
Sorry that I'm borrowing Chuta for so long.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.630
It's fine... I don't care if he just 
stays in Division 4 from now on.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.170
That would actually make me very happy.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.770
Um, is Officer Kokonose...

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:17.000
He's... on something of an investigation.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.220
Oh, look at the time. I've got to go.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.550
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:27.280
You're late, Veeyan.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.430
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:29.420
Beeyan?

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:30.970
Beeyan because his name is Vega.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.470
Oh, this is your first time 
meeting Takkun, right?

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:34.810
Ah, yes.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.730
Nice to meet you, Senpai.

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:38.340
Hi...

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:41.580
Though Love is actually way older than him.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:43.320
Well, he is 500 years old...

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:45.240
Well, let's go.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.030
I'm so excited.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:07.890
Yeah.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:12.430
Just how childish are they, 
turning red just from looking at that?

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:14.890
Hey, doesn't this look like Ninotchka-chan?

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:16.470
Hey, Chuta.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.730
N-Now that you mention it,

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:21.130
I think you might be right.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:23.490
Chuta, your heart rate is high.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.620
This one is Misuzu Sonokata.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.120
Indeed. It does look like her.

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.420
That means...

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.960
That's super convincing!

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.310
Well, there's nothing strange about 
Dr. Love having seen everyone's body.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.970
This one is Veronica-chan.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.850
So audacious.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:50.680
Indeed. It matches.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:51.970
Really?!

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:54.270
What are you talking about?!

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:54.870
Huh?

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:56.950
Veronica!

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.030
Hey, so you girls came, as well.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.370
I have a much hotter body than that!

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:02.750
Much more?!

00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:04.910
Wh-What are they doing here?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.660
It's not me! I didn't tell them anything.

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:11.910
Guys are so stupid. 
Look at them, breathing so hard.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.620
I've known for a long time that 
Officer Kokonose was a pervert.

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.780
Wha... That's not...

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.930
You can't really say 
anything back this time.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:26.810
How surprising. I thought you were 
more mature, Vega-san.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:30.610
He's the same! He's not much older Chuta.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.760
W-Well, you know... 
I'm just here as a guardian.

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.010
Wow, making excuses. Pathetic.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:37.410
You're awful.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.270
Why are guys always like this?

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:39.870
Do you have to go that far?

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.270
Disappear without leaving a trace.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.620
<b>ēlDLIVE is hiding what happened 
at the Mount Taketori incident</b>

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:49.490
ēlDLIVE is hiding what happened 
at the Mount Taketori incident?

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.750
<b>Mudslide Occurs on Mount Taketori 
During Outing</b>

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:56.500
Displaying your badge's monitor in a place
where civilians gather is against the rules.

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:06.890
Captain, we have a telegram from HQ.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.720
Bring it up.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.650
It looks like there's a new plan 
for us to head to Earth again.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:21.950
Huh... I wonder why our boss is so obsessed 
with a remote planet like that?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.420
I wonder if there's treasure there.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:31.430
<i>And the reason why DeMille saved me 
at Mount Taketori is still a mystery...</i>

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:36.290
This time, we're invading Earth for real!

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:41.610
<i>This isn't good. I need to 
hurry up and tell Chuta.</i>

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:52.980
<b>Vega Victor</b>

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.950
I wonder what this email is about.

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:03.110
Does this mean that ēlDLIVE 
knows something about

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:05.360
the Mount Taketori incident 
and is hiding it?

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:08.230
But Laine hasn't said anything.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:11.430
Is this supposed to be top secret, too?

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:12.120
Whoa, there.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.540
S-Sorry.

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:16.930
It's fine.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.370
Chuta, look!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.340
<b>Nude Art Exhibit</b>

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.420
Oh, this is...

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.030
From when we all went to the art museum.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:27.160
Are these research documents, too?

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:28.630
O-Of course.

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:33.540
Well, you know, we need to know about 
Earth's culture when we're investigating.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:35.060
<b>Nude 
Art 
Exhibit</b>

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:35.060
That's definitely a lie.

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:40.830
Do you ever have any doubts 
about ēlDLIVE, Vega?

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.610
Where did that come from?

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:48.570
For example... if they knew valuable 
information and didn't tell you...

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:52.620
It's true that management 
tends to hide things.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.870
But I think that if you 
have time to have doubts,

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:59.250
you'd be better off doing some
 investigating on your own.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.450
Investigating on my own...

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:05.840
What's the current case? 
Does it involve DeMille?

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:06.920
Yeah.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:11.140
As long as they exist in space, 
there'll never be true peace.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:16.770
If it's to eradicate them, 
I might even give up my life.

00:13:20.640 --> 00:13:22.520
What are you planning to do, Chuta?

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.780
First, I'm going to find the person 
who sent me that message.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:31.540
<b>ēlDLIVE is hiding what happened 
at the Mount Taketori incident</b>

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:31.530
If I look into where this message came from, 
I might be able to find some clues.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:33.910
You're not going to report to Laine?

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.560
Even if I did, he wouldn't tell me anything.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.350
Vega said it, too.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.780
It's better if I investigate on my own.

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.350
Since it was sent to my police badge,

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:49.790
the sender is one of the personnel
 aboard the <i>Jeanrenoi-R</i>.

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:50.600
<b>ēlDLIVE is hiding what happened 
at the Mount Taketori incident</b>

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.660
What is it?

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:55.260
The communication device is malfunctioning!

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:57.690
The SPH compass system 
has stopped working.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.350
Méliès, what happened?

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.390
Chief, this is a computer virus.

00:14:03.390 --> 00:14:04.070
Where did it originate?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.560
From the data processing room.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.610
Isolate the main system!

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:09.460
Switch over to the backup system!

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:10.310
Yoyosa!

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.960
Security team, hurry over to 
the data processing room!

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:18.270
Officer Kokonose?

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:19.530
Y-Yes?

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.940
The origin is Chuta's police badge?

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:23.660
It can't be...

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:28.530
Officer Kokonose is saying that 
he only connected to the terminal

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.130
to confirm the sender of 
an email that he got.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:32.650
Email?

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:34.140
Now what?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.760
There's a huge heat source reading.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.890
It's right in front of the <i>Jeanrenoi-R.</i>

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.770
What's that ship?

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:50.360
It should be impossible to warp out
 this close to another ship.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:53.600
They apparently targeted us in the 
brief window when were switching systems

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:58.130
because of the virus, 
while the SPH monitoring radar was off.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.710
There's a high-energy reading 
within the ship.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.510
Chief, that's...

00:15:02.510 --> 00:15:04.000
Emergency evasive maneuvers!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.610
Damage report!

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:11.500
There's a lot of damage to 
the port-side engine.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.380
The community safety section 
has several wounded!

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:16.720
<i>This is the engine room! 
Requesting immediate aid!</i>

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.140
Wh-What the?!

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.480
Send the rescue squad 
to tend to the wounded!

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:18.540
Wh-What happened?

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:22.430
This is a message for ēlDLIVE.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:27.980
I am the DeMille Solar System 
Commander, DeMille Junior.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.440
DeMille?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.700
That was quite the introduction.

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.700
I don't like formalities.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.980
What's your goal?

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:41.410
I'm sure you want something if you stopped 
your attack while we're in this state.

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:44.540
Impressive, Chief. 
You understand quickly.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:50.790
Hand over the Monitalien that's in your possession, 
along with its host, Chuta Kokonose.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:54.770
If you resist, we will target Earth 
and start our attack.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:55.690
No...

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:58.470
What do you plan to do with the Monitalien?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:02.190
Let's just say that the updated 
Monitalien is valuable to us.

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:05.350
Did you really think we'd comply 
with such demands?

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:10.070
Your power has already been pushed 
to its limits. Resistance is futile.

00:16:11.850 --> 00:16:16.380
True, with our current equipment, 
it'd be impossible to compete with them.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.940
However, I still have research facilities 
left all over Earth.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:26.530
With that equipment, it's possible 
to attack the exoatmosphere.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:30.090
Shutting down the main gun of 
a DeMille ship would be easy.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.590
Chief, make your decision.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:41.340
There's no need to even think about this. 
You don't have any choice in this matter.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.850
Right... It seems that way.

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.990
There was only one answer to begin with.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:50.500
Everyone to their battle stations!

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:52.600
Our target's right in front of us, 
the DeMille ship!

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:54.140
Yoyosa!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.270
Fire volley!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.870
Dr. Love.

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:01.400
Okay.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:11.210
All right!

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.120
We did it!

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:15.020
What's wrong?

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:20.340
Well, it appears that DeMille ships 
have appeared all across the Earth.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.500
So it wasn't just one ship?

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.300
They put one over on us.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:27.240
I told you that resistance was futile.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.190
I'll give you one hour.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:32.850
You need to hand over the Monitalien 
and Chuta Kokonose by then.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:36.590
Once the time comes, 
we will attack the Earth.

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:41.040
An hour...

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.280
We can't do anything in an hour.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.660
It's almost going to be 59 minutes.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:50.530
This all happened because of Chuta! 
Maybe he's connected with DeMille.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:51.550
Of course he isn't!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.910
Calm down.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:56.380
Chief Laine!

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:00.670
This... This is all my fault, right?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.020
Chuta...

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:08.130
Because of me, 
everyone on Earth is in danger.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:10.020
Calm down, Chuta.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.620
Everyone...

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:17.280
I should just go to DeMille. 
That'll solve everything.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:19.110
Chuta...

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:23.960
Chief, hurry and hand me over to DeMille.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.780
Get a hold of yourself, chu!

00:18:28.780 --> 00:18:32.290
This isn't just your problem anymore, 
Officer Kokonose.

00:18:33.450 --> 00:18:35.790
Assistant Inspector Chips...

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:41.850
Chief. Why don't we transfer 
Officer Kokonose to Earth, just in case?

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:42.510
Huh?

00:18:42.920 --> 00:18:46.180
We can keep him out of sight from DeMille's
better there than we can here.

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:49.170
Right... Chips.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:52.100
Go to the Space Café 
and hide along with Chuta.

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:53.940
Don't make any moves until I give the order.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.010
Yoyosa!

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:56.160
P-Please wait!

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:00.440
Chu...

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:10.040
There isn't a single person around, chu. 
This is a huge deal, chu.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:12.890
Officer Kokonose?

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:19.300
<b>Shirobori Middle School</b>

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:23.050
<b>HIROBORI 
Bowl</b>

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:26.060
<b>Shizuoka Aoi Art Museum</b>

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:26.060
<b>Special Exhibit</b>

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.990
<b>Temporarily Closed
Dear Chuta, I've taken shelter 
in the school's gymnasium. 
When you see this...</b>

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.440
<i>Dear Chuta...</i>

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:40.990
<i>I've gone to the school's 
gymnasium for shelter.</i>

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.860
Sounds like Mimi is safe.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:44.990
It's happening again...

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:48.460
I did something that I shouldn't have again.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:49.910
Chuta...

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:54.420
I'm starting to disappear. 
Don't lose your confidence, Chuta!

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:58.280
I... How could I have...

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.460
What's going on?

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:09.180
What is this?

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.350
It's Gucchi!

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.100
Huh?

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:17.890
I can read it... Gucchi must have 
written this message.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.520
What does it say?

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:24.000
"DeMille is on the move. They're after...

00:20:24.000 --> 00:20:25.050
Dolugh."

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:30.120
"And there's a spy within ēlDLIVE."

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:35.080
"Be extremely careful. The spy's name is..."

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.220
Dolugh? What's wrong, Dolugh?

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.710
Dolugh!

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:42.330
Dolugh!

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:47.120
D-Dolugh...

00:20:57.010 --> 00:20:57.930
Chuta.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.880
You were told to hide in the 
Space Café, weren't you?

00:21:03.470 --> 00:21:04.460
Vega...

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:06.770
What should I do?

00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:08.730
Chuta...

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:14.350
Hey, tell me. What would you do 
at a time like this?

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.320
Well, I would...

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:18.960
Officer Kokonose.

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:22.000
What are you doing here?

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.830
The same as you, Inspector Vega.

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:26.770
I was worried about Officer Kokonose,

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.730
and I'm sure everyone 
at the bureau is, as well.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:32.730
No one cares about me one way or another...

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:36.590
You know, don't you, Sonokata?

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:40.370
I was involved in an accident 
on Mount Taketori in the past.

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:45.280
And one of my friends ended up 
an executive officer at DeMille.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:49.420
It wouldn't be weird if ēlDLIVE 
was looking into all of this, would it?

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:54.960
But Chief Laine, along with everyone else, 
won't tell me anything.

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:57.240
Officer Kokonose.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:04.210
Chief Laine gave this to me. I'm sorry 
that I couldn't give it to you sooner.

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:10.540
This is ēlDLIVE's complete case file concerning 
the incident on Mount Taketori.

00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:17.430
I knew right after Chuta joined that the 
Mount Taketori incident was in ēlDLIVE's jurisdiction.

00:22:17.640 --> 00:22:22.640
But one of his friends was alive, and ended up 
working for DeMille, of all things.

00:22:23.300 --> 00:22:26.450
I'm sure he's pretty confused 
about all of this, too.

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:30.290
I wanted to eventually tell him 
when the time was right, but...

00:22:31.190 --> 00:22:36.340
As you said, Officer Kokonose, the details 
surrounding that case are still unknown.

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:40.720
But it appears that it's been confirmed 
that aliens are somehow involved.

00:22:46.850 --> 00:22:50.580
Chief Laine thought that much about me?

00:22:51.530 --> 00:22:53.290
And yet, I...

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:54.820
Officer Kokonose.

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:59.650
The one thing that you can do 
right now is protect the Earth

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:02.100
as a member of ēlDLIVE.

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:10.680
That's right. I can't give up just yet!

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:27.790
That's right. I can't give up just yet.

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:31.750
I'm going to get through this 
as a member of ēlDLIVE.

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:33.790
Let's go, Sonokata!

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:35.430
Next time on <i>ēlDLIVE,</i>

00:23:35.430 --> 00:23:36.760
"Our sympathy."

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:39.130
We'll protect the Earth, no matter what!
